    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2FVFDA4BhYwYUqzWKVLmVVB)_\n\n**Before:** an agent had no way to run or check the Emacs config in a cloud container. Booting `init.el` stalls there, because Elpaca needs MELPA and GNU ELPA, which that environment blocks.\n\n**After:** `.config/emacs-modular/.claude/skills/run-emacs-modular/` holds a skill, a driver and a harness:\n- `driver.sh report` loads every default module and prints ok/FAILED per module (59 ok, 13 failed here, the failures being modules whose packages are absent).\n- `driver.sh eval FORM MOD…` evaluates a form after requiring modules.\n- `driver.sh test FILE` runs an ERT file against the loaded modules.\n\n**How:** the harness sources `early-init.el` but not `init.el`, turns `use-package` `:ensure` into a no-op and requires modules one by one. It works on a throwaway copy of the config, with an empty notes folder.\n\n**Not verified:** a full boot with packages, the GUI, keybindings, Magit and TRAMP. Those need MELPA/ELPA access or the Mac (`emacs-pr`). The `report`, `eval` and `test` commands were run in this container with Emacs 29.3.\n\nBranch name: PR number assumed to be #42 when pushed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_019StSDiUybvbjofpuYJW4mE)_",
